    <comment>Although the Bunsen burner flame bends and stretches, the stretch effect mainly comes from the curvature part at the flame's tip [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2015.11.120]. Natarajan et al. [https://doi.org/10.1016/j.combustflame.2007.05.003] found that the flame-area method reduces the effects of flame-bending on flame speed and is in close agreement with the unstretched SL.</comment>
